drm/msm/a6xx: leave RBBM_NC_MODE_CNTL at its reset value on A650 (TEST)

Holodor (2026-10-01), RP5 DXVK whole-SoC freeze investigation. Downstream KGSL
(msm-4.19 adreno_a6xx.c, kona) never writes RBBM_NC_MODE_CNTL on A650; mainline
writes the UBWC config's macrotile_mode (1 = 8-channel). Every other UBWC register
(RB/TPL1/SP_NC_MODE_CNTL, UCHE_MODE_CNTL) is bit-identical to KGSL once HBB is 15
(0700/0701). Logs the reset value once. TEST patch - keep only if it stops the freeze.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
@@ -873,6 +873,17 @@
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A6XX_UCHE_MODE_CNTL,
 		  min_acc_len_64b << 23 | hbb_lo << 21);
 
+	/*
+	 * Downstream KGSL never writes RBBM_NC_MODE_CNTL on A650 and leaves the
+	 * reset value (4-channel macrotiling per its own comment); match it.
+	 */
+	if (adreno_is_a650(adreno_gpu)) {
+		dev_info_once(&gpu->pdev->dev,
+			      "A650: RBBM_NC_MODE_CNTL left at reset value %#x\n",
+			      gpu_read(gpu, REG_A6XX_RBBM_NC_MODE_CNTL));
+		return;
+	}
+
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A6XX_RBBM_NC_MODE_CNTL,
 		  cfg->macrotile_mode);
 }
